  "body": "Step [14.9](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#javascript-protocol) says \"Let result be the result of running the classic script script.\". It links to [run a classic script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#run-a-classic-script) which states \"Let realm be settings's Realm.\".\n\nNo settings were specified or mentioned in the preceding steps (lest I missed it) so it's unclear what the realm is.\n\nWith iframes, Firefox will use the resulting's iframe's realm (doing something like `<iframe src=\"javascript:this.x=5,'<script>console.log(x);</script>'\";` works there) while chrome seems to use a temporary realm.\n\nDid I miss it or are steps missing?\n",
